0'\n\nBy\n\nTD\n\nTracing No.\n\nL - 14903\n\nSheet No.\n\nC-2\nPage 12 of 45","ocr":false},{"page":13,"text":"VINEYARD PLANNING COMMISSION STAFF REPORT\n\nMeeting Date: October 7, 2026\n\nAgenda Item: PLAN26-0011 Site Plan Application - Minor Amendment Orchards Phase 7\n\nDepartment: Planning\n\nPresenter:\n\nAnthony Fletcher\n\nBackground/Discussion:\n\nSummary\nThe applicant is requesting an amendment to the approved site plan for The Orchards Phase 7,\naffecting Buildings 53 through 64. The proposed modifications include changes to selected unit\nlayouts, Level 2 decks, and storefront colors.\n\nProposed Changes\n• Conversion of covered decks to bedrooms: In Buildings 53, 55, 56, 58, 59, and 61, the\nexterior covered decks associated with Units J and K would be enclosed and converted\ninto additional bedrooms. Windows would be installed within the former deck openings.\n\nThe exterior siding and roof design would remain unchanged.\n• Unit Type D deck modification: In all buildings, the Level 2 deck for Unit Type D would\nbe revised by creating an opening in the original brick wall and installing a railing. The\napplicant states that this change would improve interior visibility and natural light while\nsupporting better deck drainage.\n• Storefront color change: The storefront color would be changed from dark bronze to\nwhite throughout the project to provide consistency with the other buildings in the\ndevelopment.\n\nFiscal Impact:\n\nN/A\n\nRecommendation:\nStaff recommends approval of these proposed changes as this would maintain consistency in\nelevation and material use throughout the development.\n\nSample Motion:\n\"I move to approve PLAN26-0011 Site Plan Amendment Application — Orchards Phase 7 as\npresented and discussed\"\n\nAttachments:\n\n1.\n\nThe_Orchards_Phase_7-_Buildings_Narrative\n\n2.\nPhase 7 Elevations_The_Orchards_Townhome_-_Building_59_Revision_2_and_4_comparison\nPage 13 of 45","ocr":false},{"page":14,"text":"Page 14 of 45","ocr":false},{"page":15,"text":"Vineyard City Planning Department\n\n707 East Mill Road,\n\nSuite 202\n\nVineyard, Utah\n\nAttn:\n\nAnthony\n\nThe Orchards Phase 7: Building 53\n\nThe following modifications were directed have been made from the\noriginal design originally proposed.\n\nThe purpose of the change was that ownership opted to provide an\nadditional bedroom instead of the exterior covered deck\n\nPlease review the plans to see the notation of the change. The following\nis a summary of those changes.\n• The Two Units affected are the Unit K and Unit J only.\n• The change was to infill the openings around the deck which has\nbeen converted into a bedroom. The room is now enclosed, with\nwindows installed in the locations where the deck openings were\npreviously located.\n• The exterior siding and roof remain unchanged.\n•\n\nFor Unit Type D, the Level 2 deck has been revised to include a\nopening in the original brick wall with a railing, providing improved\nvisibility and light to the interior while allowing for more positive\ndeck drainage.\n\n•\n\nThe storefront color has been changed from dark bronze to white\nto maintain consistency with the other buildings throughout the\ndevelopment.\n\nNot all buildings on site have all the changes, therefore see the following\nbreak down for each building.\n\nThe Orchards Phase 7: Building 54\n\nThe only items included with Building 54 were the decks at Unit D.\n•\n\nFor Unit Type D, the Level 2 deck has been revised to include a\nopening in the original brick wall with a railing, providing improved\nvisibility and light to the interior while allowing for more positive\ndeck drainage.\n\n•\n\nThe storefront color has been changed from dark bronze to white\nto maintain consistency with the other buildings throughout the\ndevelopment.\n\nPage 15 of 45","ocr":false},{"page":16,"text":"The Orchards Phase 7: Building 55\n\nThe following modifications were directed have been made from the\noriginal design originally proposed.\n\nThe